const e="taunton-festival-acting",d=2027,a="The template cites the 2026 Drama Syllabus; the festival has since published the Drama Syllabus 2027 (file Drama-Syllabus-2027-V2.pdf, linked from its Drama Festival page), so the 2027 edition is used for rules, dates, venue, contacts, fees and times. Read both whole (8 pages each) and the festival's Drama Festival web page. Differences found: time limits are now per class (Solo and Duo Acting 3 minutes up to Year 8 and 4 minutes from Year 9; the template installs the 2026 flat 3 minutes), a new rule on explicit content, time limits no longer include set-up, and the Redirection Acting classes are not printed in the 2027 syllabus; their rows are written from the 2026 syllabus and marked as 2026 only. Group Acting, Performance Sight Reading and Shakespeare are in the syllabus but not in this template, so each has one line under 'other'; the rest of the syllabus (Poetry, Reading, Public Speaking, Improvisation, Mime) is named there too. Placed: marking system and categories, certificates, trophies, safeguarding rules, parking. Not copied: the trophy return street address (it is a private farm address; the page says only that trophies can be left in the porch, the address is in the syllabus), the postal address for the Friends scheme, the lists of benefactors and life members, the chairman's foreword and the adjudicator's biography. The syllabus does NOT print: points per placing, an entry fee per audience session beyond the 2.50 pounds charge, or a refund rule other than the withdrawal of a class. The festival web page says entries close in October 2026; the syllabus gives the exact date, which is used (it has already passed on 2026-10-15). Fees are in pounds sterling and kept in Variables.",t={Title:"Rules & Criteria",Subtitle:"Taunton Festival of the Arts, Drama Festival 2027. Read these rules before you enter.",NoticeTitle:"Please Read Before Registering",Notice:"The Drama Festival is on {{FestivalDates}} at {{Venue}}. Entries open {{EntryOpens}} and close {{EntryCloses}}. Enter and pay through the online booking system. Entries cannot be processed until payment has been made.",Notes:["In classes with an age limit, the relevant date is {{AgeCutoffDate}}.","Time limits include any introduction. They do not include setting up or clearing a set or props.","No photography, video or audio recording is allowed.","Mobile phones must be turned off in the auditorium."],Sections:[{Key:"general",Title:"General Rules",Items:["The Drama Festival is part of the Taunton Festival of the Arts. It is a chance to perform and also a chance for young people to learn, grow and develop their creativity.","The festival is affiliated to the British and International Federation of Festivals and is a registered charity.","The Committee may accept or refuse entries, cancel or change any class, or merge one or more classes, especially where there are very few entries.","Digital programmes are sent to competitors before the festival.","Mobile phones must be turned off while you are in the auditorium.","Smoking is not allowed in any of the venues. This includes e-cigarettes and vaping devices.","Teachers and parents must be aware of their duties when they enter performers with limited physical ability or special needs, bearing in mind the limits of the performing areas.","The teacher or parent must pass to the adjudicator, through the organiser, any information that could affect the adjudicator's work.","Any performance with explicit content must be announced with a warning. The audience must be given the chance to leave the auditorium before the performance begins.","A performer who does not give the audience a fair warning is asked to stop and may not be allowed to continue.","Explicit content includes, but is not limited to, swearing, sexual references, references to drug or alcohol use, references to extreme violence, and derogatory, misogynistic, racist or homophobic language.","The Committee is not responsible for any injury to a performer or a member of the public on festival premises. It is not responsible for loss or damage to property during the festival.","Lost property: the Committee cannot accept responsibility for property left at a venue during the festival."]},{Key:"eligibility",Title:"Eligibility",Items:["Classes are set by school year, such as Year 4 and Under, Year 7 and 8 or Sixth Form. Open classes have no age limit.","In classes with an age limit, the relevant date is {{AgeCutoffDate}}.","A performer may enter both an acting class and a redirection class, but must not perform the same monologue, duologue or scene in both classes (2026 syllabus; see the note on Redirection Acting).","Class entries are for performers who bring the performance themselves: the monologue, duologue or scene is of the performer's own choosing."]},{Key:"registration",Title:"How to Register",Items:["Entries open on {{EntryOpens}} and close on {{EntryCloses}}.","Enter through the online booking system on the festival website ({{FestivalWebsite}}).","Entries cannot be processed until payment has been made. Payments are taken through the online booking system.","The festival may close entry early without giving a reason.","Digital programmes are sent to competitors before the festival.","For questions, contact the Speech and Drama Secretary: {{DramaSecretary}}."]},{Key:"fees",Title:"Fees and Payment",Items:["Entry fees are per class, in pounds sterling. They are listed with each competition.","Entries cannot be processed until payment has been made.","Payments are taken through the online booking system on the festival website.","Only if a class is withdrawn is the fee refunded.","Audience entry charge: {{AudienceCharge}}."]},{Key:"dates",Title:"Dates",Items:["The Drama Festival is on {{FestivalDates}}. The class timings are to be confirmed.","Entries open on {{EntryOpens}} and close on {{EntryCloses}}.","Some performers, not only prize winners, may be asked to perform at other festival events, including the TFA Gala on {{GalaDate}}.","Drama trophies must be returned by {{TrophyReturnDate}}."]},{Key:"venue",Title:"Venue and Parking",Items:["The venue is {{Venue}}.","Parking near the venue: {{Parking}}."]},{Key:"points",Title:"Marks and Categories",Items:["Numerical marks are awarded for drama. The adjudicator places each competitor in one of seven categories.","65 to 69, Developing: a performance that shows an awareness of technical skills and needs more consistency and artistry.","70 to 74, Progressing: a performance that shows development of technique and, or, communication and commitment.","75 to 79, Merit: a competent performance that shows some artistic awareness and, or, technical ability.","80 to 84, Commended: a convincing performance technically and artistically, with increasing style and communication skills.","85 to 89, Honours: an excellent performance that shows fluent technical and artistic skills with emerging individuality.","90 to 94, Outstanding: an impressive performance technically and artistically, with spontaneity and clear individuality.","95 and over, Exceptional: a superlative performance that shows exceptional artistic individuality."]},{Key:"prizes",Title:"Prizes, Trophies and Certificates",Items:["The Class Winner is always decided and announced. The adjudicator also announces second and third.","The categories of other competitors are not usually announced. They are shown on the adjudicator's comment sheet that each performer receives.","Certificates are awarded for all entries.","Drama trophies are not given for every class. A trophy may not be awarded if the standard is not thought high enough.","Trophies may be withheld, withdrawn, recalled or given to someone else at the Committee's choice.","Trophy winners are expected to have their trophies engraved at their own cost.","Drama trophies won in the festival must be polished and returned by {{TrophyReturnDate}}. The return address is given in the syllabus, and trophies can be left in the porch."]},{Key:"conduct",Title:"Conduct and Safeguarding",Items:["No photography, video or audio recording is allowed. This is the Safeguarding policy. An authorised photographer may be available.","The Committee is not responsible for unsupervised children. Parents and teachers must take full responsibility for their children and pupils on festival premises and must not let them stray from the designated areas (Safeguarding Policy).","A performance that has explicit content must be announced with a warning first."]},{Key:"judging",Title:"Judging and Time Limits",Items:["Where a time limit is given, going over it will lead to the adjudicator stopping the performance.","The time allowed includes any introduction. It does not include setting up or clearing a set or props."]},{Key:"other",Title:"Other Classes in the Syllabus",Items:["Poetry: Solo Performance Poetry and Verse Speaking (Year 1 and under to Open, 2 minutes), Duo Performance Poetry (2 minutes), Group Performance Poetry (5 minutes), Solo Performance Poetry Own Composition (no more than 120 words, 2 minutes) and Spoken Word (2 minutes). Poems are own choice or from the TFA Poetry Anthology.","Reading: Solo Spoken Prose (3 minutes), Solo Prepared Reading (1 minute), Solo Reading of Religious Texts (1 minute), Solo Sight Reading (1 minute) and Solo TV News Reading (3 minutes).","Public Speaking: Solo Project Speaking (3 minutes).","Performance Arts: Prepared Improvisation (2 minutes), Unprepared Improvisation (1 minute) and Mime (2 minutes, no props).","Acting classes not in this template: Group Acting (5 minutes, every member of the group must have a speaking part), Performance Sight Reading (a new scene with 5 minutes to rehearse) and Shakespeare (2 minutes for solo and duo, 5 minutes for a group).","Friends and Benefactors: anyone may support music, drama and dance for young people by becoming a Friend or Benefactor of the festival, from {{FriendsFee}} a year. Ask at {{FriendsContact}}.","Stewards: to help with stewarding, contact {{StewardsContact}}."]}],Documents:[{Title:"Drama Syllabus 2027 (PDF)",Url:"https://www.tauntonfestival.org.uk/s/Drama-Syllabus-2027-V2.pdf"},{Title:"TFA Poetry Anthology (PDF)",Url:"https://www.tauntonfestival.org.uk/s/Drama-Anthology-2026.pdf"},{Title:"Drama Festival page and online entry",Url:"https://www.tauntonfestival.org.uk/drama-festival"}]},n=[],r=[],s=[{Title:"Solo Acting",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 p.12, Category One",Sections:{About:["The performer gives a prepared monologue of their own choosing."],TimeAndFormat:["Time limit: 3 minutes up to Year 8, 4 minutes from Year 9. The time includes any introduction."],Rules:null,Allowed:["Props are permitted."],NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["Classes and fees: {{SoloActingFees}}."]},Markdown:`## About this competition
- The performer gives a prepared monologue of their own choosing.

## Time and format
- Time limit: 3 minutes up to Year 8, 4 minutes from Year 9. The time includes any introduction.

## Allowed
- Props are permitted.

## Notes for participants
- Classes and fees: {{SoloActingFees}}.`},{Title:"Duo Acting",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 pp.12-13, Category Two",Sections:{About:["Two performers give a prepared duologue or scene of their own choosing."],TimeAndFormat:["Time limit: 3 minutes up to Year 8, 4 minutes from Year 9. The time includes any introduction."],Rules:null,Allowed:["Props are permitted."],NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["Classes and fees: {{DuoActingFees}}."]},Markdown:`## About this competition
- Two performers give a prepared duologue or scene of their own choosing.

## Time and format
- Time limit: 3 minutes up to Year 8, 4 minutes from Year 9. The time includes any introduction.

## Allowed
- Props are permitted.

## Notes for participants
- Classes and fees: {{DuoActingFees}}.`},{Title:"Redirection Acting - Solo",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2026 pp.12-13, Category Three (not in the 2027 syllabus)",Sections:{About:["This class is printed in the 2026 syllabus only. The 2027 syllabus does not list it. Check with the organiser before you use it.","The performer gives a prepared scene from memory. The adjudicator then gives notes and redirects the scene, and the performer plays it again."],TimeAndFormat:["In 2026 every drama class had a maximum time of 3 minutes per entry."],Rules:["A performer may enter both an acting class and a redirection class but must not perform the same monologue in both classes."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:["Marks are given for the first performance and also for how well the performer responds to the redirection."],Points:null,Notes:["2026 classes and fees: {{RedirectionFees}}."]},Markdown:`## About this competition
- This class is printed in the 2026 syllabus only. The 2027 syllabus does not list it. Check with the organiser before you use it.
- The performer gives a prepared scene from memory. The adjudicator then gives notes and redirects the scene, and the performer plays it again.

## Time and format
- In 2026 every drama class had a maximum time of 3 minutes per entry.

## Rules
- A performer may enter both an acting class and a redirection class but must not perform the same monologue in both classes.

## Judging
- Marks are given for the first performance and also for how well the performer responds to the redirection.

## Notes for participants
- 2026 classes and fees: {{RedirectionFees}}.`},{Title:"Redirection Acting - Duo",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2026 pp.12-13, Category Three (not in the 2027 syllabus)",Sections:{About:["This class is printed in the 2026 syllabus only. The 2027 syllabus does not list it. Check with the organiser before you use it.","The performers give a prepared scene from memory. The adjudicator then gives notes and redirects the scene, and the performers play it again."],TimeAndFormat:["In 2026 every drama class had a maximum time of 3 minutes per entry."],Rules:["Performers may enter both an acting class and a redirection class but must not perform the same duologue or scene in both classes."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:["Marks are given for the first performance and also for how well the performers respond to the redirection."],Points:null,Notes:["2026 classes and fees: {{RedirectionFees}}."]},Markdown:`## About this competition
- This class is printed in the 2026 syllabus only. The 2027 syllabus does not list it. Check with the organiser before you use it.
- The performers give a prepared scene from memory. The adjudicator then gives notes and redirects the scene, and the performers play it again.

## Time and format
- In 2026 every drama class had a maximum time of 3 minutes per entry.

## Rules
- Performers may enter both an acting class and a redirection class but must not perform the same duologue or scene in both classes.

## Judging
- Marks are given for the first performance and also for how well the performers respond to the redirection.

## Notes for participants
- 2026 classes and fees: {{RedirectionFees}}.`}],o=[],i=[{Key:"FestivalDates",Kind:"date",Label:"Drama Festival dates",Value:"Monday 1 February to Wednesday 3 February 2027",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 p.1"},{Key:"EntryOpens",Kind:"date",Label:"Entry opening date",Value:"Monday 7 September 2026",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 p.1"},{Key:"EntryCloses",Kind:"date",Label:"Entry closing date",Value:"Friday 9 October 2026",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 p.1"},{Key:"AgeCutoffDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Date used for age-limit classes",Value:"1 September 2026",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 p.4 rule 2"},{Key:"GalaDate",Kind:"date",Label:"TFA Gala",Value:"Sunday 13 June 2027",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 p.5"},{Key:"TrophyReturnDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date to return drama trophies",Value:"End of November 2027",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 pp.2 and 4"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Venue",Value:{Name:"Temple Methodist Church",Address:"Upper High Street",City:"Taunton TA1 3PY, Somerset, England",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Drama Festival web page and Drama Syllabus 2027 p.14"},{Key:"Parking",Kind:"text",Label:"Nearby car parks",Value:"Orchard Multi Storey Car Park, Paul Street, TA1 3XZ (open 7am-7pm Monday-Saturday, 8am-5.30pm Sunday); High Street Car Park, Old Pig Market off Paul Street, TA1 3PB (charges 8am-6pm Monday-Saturday); Crescent Car Park, The Crescent, TA1 4ED (charges 8am-6pm Monday-Saturday, maximum stay 4 hours); Fons George Car Park, Fons George, TA1 3JT (charges 8am-6pm Monday-Saturday, maximum stay 4 hours)",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 p.14"},{Key:"FestivalWebsite",Kind:"link",Label:"Festival website and online booking",Value:"https://www.tauntonfestival.org.uk",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 pp.1 and 4"},{Key:"DramaSecretary",Kind:"contact",Label:"Speech and Drama Secretary",Value:{Name:"Laura Sewell",Role:"Speech & Drama Secretary",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"laurasewell76@gmail.com"},Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 p.2"},{Key:"StewardsContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Stewards Organiser",Value:{Name:"Matthew Kirby",Role:"Stewards Organiser",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"mattakirby@aol.com"},Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 p.3"},{Key:"FriendsContact",Kind:"contact",Label:"Friends and Benefactors scheme",Value:{Name:"Taunton Festival of the Arts Friends and Benefactors",Role:"Friend and Benefactor Secretary: Lisa Simpson",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"tfafandb@gmail.com"},Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 pp.2-3"},{Key:"Adjudicator",Kind:"text",Label:"Drama adjudicator",Value:"Rosalind Taylor",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 p.7"},{Key:"AudienceCharge",Kind:"fee",Label:"Entry charge for the audience",Value:"2.50 pounds",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 p.1"},{Key:"FriendsFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Friend or Benefactor level, from",Value:"20 pounds",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 p.3"},{Key:"SoloActingFees",Kind:"fee",Label:"Solo Acting classes and fees",Value:"A31 Year 4 & Under 6 pounds; A32 Year 5 & 6 6 pounds; A33 Year 7 & 8 6.50 pounds; A34 Year 9, 10 & 11 7 pounds; A35 Sixth Form 7.50 pounds; A36 Open 8 pounds",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 p.12"},{Key:"DuoActingFees",Kind:"fee",Label:"Duo Acting classes and fees",Value:"A37 Year 4 & Under 12 pounds; A38 Year 5 & 6 12 pounds; A39 Year 7 & 8 13 pounds; A40 Year 9, 10 & 11 14 pounds; A41 Sixth Form 15 pounds; A42 Open 16 pounds",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2027 pp.12-13"},{Key:"RedirectionFees",Kind:"fee",Label:"Redirection Acting classes and fees (2026 syllabus)",Value:"Solo: A45 Year 7 & 8 6.50 pounds; A46 Year 9, 10 & 11 7 pounds; A47 Open 8 pounds. Duo: A48 Year 7 & 8 6.50 pounds; A49 Year 9, 10 & 11 7 pounds; A50 Open 8 pounds. Group: A51 Open 20 pounds",Source:"Drama Syllabus 2026 p.13"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"News printed for the 2027 festival",Value:[{Date:"",Title:"2027 class timings",Text:"Class timings for each festival day (Monday 1, Tuesday 2 and Wednesday 3 February 2027, all at Temple Methodist Church) are to be confirmed. Contact the Drama Secretary with any questions.",Url:"https://www.tauntonfestival.org.uk/drama-festival"},{Date:"",Title:"Entry may close early",Text:"Taunton Festival of the Arts keeps the right to close entry to the festival or competition early without further explanation.",Url:""}],Source:"Drama Festival web page"}],l=[{Claim:"Dates, entry dates, rules, marking system, trophy rules, venue, contacts, per-class fees and time limits read from the festival's own 2027 Drama Syllabus, which supersedes the 2026 edition the template cites.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own circular",Source:"Taunton Festival of the Arts Drama Syllabus 2027 (V2), 8 pages",Url:"https://www.tauntonfestival.org.uk/s/Drama-Syllabus-2027-V2.pdf"},{Claim:"Redirection Acting rules and fees written from the 2026 syllabus because the 2027 syllabus does not list the class.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own circular (past edition)",Source:"Taunton Festival of the Arts Drama Syllabus 2026, pages 12-13",Url:"https://static1.squarespace.com/static/635c0bb4259a125cc54d2f6f/t/68b6d20db3435a798583dbe6/1756811789856/Drama+Syllabus+2026+FINAL.pdf"},{Claim:"Venue address and 2027 festival days read from the festival's Drama Festival page.",SourceType:"Primary - organiser's own web page",Source:"Drama Festival page",Url:"https://www.tauntonfestival.org.uk/drama-festival"}],u={TemplateKey:e,Year:2027,Note:a,Page:t,ParticipantTypes:n,AgeGroups:r,Competitions:s,CompetitionAgeGroups:o,Variables:i,Evidence:l};export{r as AgeGroups,o as CompetitionAgeGroups,s as Competitions,l as Evidence,a as Note,t as Page,n as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,i as Variables,d as Year,u as default};
